-- title:
--   Mod-p parabolic eigenclass attached to a maximal Hecke ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \ge 1$, a natural number $n$, a set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ containing every prime divisor of $N$, a prime $p$ with $p \ne 2$ and $p \nmid N$ and $n < p$, a predicate $Q$ on $\mathbb{N}$ and a function $a : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$. Let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N (n+2) S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_{n+2}(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators [`CuspForm.heckeTLin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators [`CuspForm.heckeULin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and let $\mathfrak{m} \subset \mathbb{T}$ be a maximal ideal containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$. Write $\rho$ for the representation of $\Gamma_0(N)$ on the degree-$n$ homogeneous binary forms over $\mathbb{Z}$ obtained by restricting [`HeckeEis.binaryFormRepSL ℤ n`](def/HeckeEis_BinaryFormRep.html#L61) along the inclusion $\Gamma_0(N) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $H^1_{\mathrm{par}} =$ [`HeckeEis.coeffH1par ρ`](def/Gamma0CoeffCohomology.html#L100) be the quotient of the module of parabolic $1$-cocycles (cocycles $z$ with $z(\gamma) \in \operatorname{range}(\rho(\gamma) - 1)$ whenever $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$) by the coboundaries lying in it. The conclusion asserts the existence of a class $y \in H^1_{\mathrm{par}}$ such that $y$ is not of the form $p \cdot y'$, and such that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$ and every additive endomorphism $T$ of $H^1_{\mathrm{par}}$ which is induced by [`HeckeEis.coeffHeckeFun N ℓ ρ (HeckeEis.binaryFormAlphaAdj ℤ n ℓ)`](def/Gamma0CoeffCohomology.html#L129) — meaning that for each parabolic cocycle $z$ there is a parabolic cocycle $w$ whose underlying function on $\Gamma_0(N)$ equals that Hecke transform of $z$ and with $T[z] = [w]$ — one has $T y - a(\ell) \cdot y \in p \cdot H^1_{\mathrm{par}}$.
--
--   This is the passage from a maximal ideal of the anemic Hecke algebra acting on weight $n+2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ to a mod-$p$ eigenclass in the integral parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$ with coefficients in degree-$n$ binary forms, in the style of the eigenform construction of Deligne–Serre together with the cohomological comparison of Ash–Stevens. It feeds the corresponding statement with coefficients in a field, [`HeckeEis.exists_coeffH1par_binaryFormRepSL_eigenclass_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_of_ne_two`](thm.html#HeckeEis.exists_coeffH1par_binaryFormRepSL_eigenclass_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_of_ne_two), the extra hypotheses $p \ne 2$, $p \nmid N$, $n < p$ being carried along for that consumer.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HeckeEis_exists_coeffH1par_int_modp_eigenclass_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra.lean

